The ACCDE issue is likely a compilation error somewhere in your VBA — Access won't compile to ACCDE if there are any unresolved references or syntax errors. We can fix that separately.

For the navigation bar problem right now, add this to frmMain Form_Load and Form_Activate:

vb
Private Sub Form_Load()
    DoCmd.NavigateTo "acNavigationCategoryObjectType"
    DoCmd.RunCommand acCmdWindowHide
    Application.Caption = "Macro Mega"
    CommandBars("Navigation Pane").Enabled = False
End Sub

Private Sub Form_Activate()
    CommandBars("Navigation Pane").Enabled = False
End Sub

And add this to modGlobals in your startup sub, before frmMain opens:

vb
DoCmd.ShowToolbar "Ribbon", acToolbarNo
CommandBars("Navigation Pane").Enabled = False

For the ACCDE issue — in the VBA editor go to Debug → Compile Database. It will stop at the first error and highlight it. Tell me what error it shows and we'll fix it, then try making the ACCDE again. A successful compile is the only thing blocking you from locking the whole thing down properly.
